msgid "Source: [`src/fixture/fixture.mbt`](../../../src/fixture/fixture.mbt)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:24
msgid "The examples on this page call them through their default aliases (`@model`, `@fixture`)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:27
msgid "Fixtures"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:31
msgid "`Fixture` is the lifecycle of one kind of input."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:46
#: manual/api/runner.md:262
#: manual/api/stats.md:51
#: manual/api/stats.md:162
msgid "Field"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:46
msgid "Called"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:48
msgid "once per dataset"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:48
msgid "generate the input from the context"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:49
msgid "once per dataset, and for minimized inputs"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:49
msgid "identify the input in events"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:50
msgid "before every `prepare`"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:50
msgid "protect the materialized input from mutation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:51
msgid "per the setup policy"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:51
msgid "turn a copy into what an implementation runs on; receives the implementation id"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:52
msgid "after the prepared value is used"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:52
msgid "release or restore it"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:53
msgid "how often `prepare` runs and whether it is timed"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:57
msgid "`Fixture::new` builds a fixture from all of its parts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:63
msgid "The arguments follow the field order."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:93
msgid "`Fixture::immutable` builds a fixture for inputs that are never modified."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/fixture.md:99
msgid "`clone_input` and `prepare` return their argument, `reset` does nothing, and the setup policy is `PerDataset`, `ExcludedFromMeasurement`, `DatasetWorkspace`."
